# .cybeignore: paths CybeDefend's SAST, IaC and secret scanners skip.
#
# Syntax: the same as .gitignore (comments, `dir/`, `*.ext`, `**/`, `!negation`).
# Scope: SAST, IaC and the secret pass share this filter. SCA and container
# scans do not read it.
#
# An entry here also stops secret detection on that path, now and in later
# commits. To silence one finding instead, prefer a line-level directive:
# `cybedefend-ignore[CD-SAST-<NNNN>]` silences that rule on that line only.
# Never silence a real credential: rotate it.
#
# Add an entry only with a comment saying why its findings are not real.

# ============================================
# TEST CODE
# ============================================
# Findings in tests are fixtures: placeholder keys such as 'super-secret',
# documentation example keys, regexes over message names. No test file is
# bundled into a shipped image, and the module under test sits beside it and
# stays scanned.
#
# Cost: these globs also silence secret detection across the test suite, which
# is where a real key pasted by mistake would land. Add a negation below rather
# than narrowing a glob when a test must stay under secret detection.
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.e2e-spec.ts
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.tsx
**/*.test.mjs

# Shared test fixtures read by the specs above: known-answer vectors (HKDF test
# keys), sample SARIF and SBOM reports, compose files built for tests. Their
# keys and findings are inputs to tests, never deployed.
libs/test-fixtures/

# Exception: keep this spec scanned. It tests secret redaction with literals in
# real credential shapes; keeping it under secret detection means a real key
# pasted there by mistake is still reported.
!apps/analysis-reporting-service/src/core/utils/redact-secrets.spec.ts
